<title>NORWAY: Norsk Hydro chief sees no rise in aluminium prices.</title>
<headline>Norsk Hydro chief sees no rise in aluminium prices.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian industrial giant Norsk Hydro ASA said on Wednesday it did not expect aluminium prices to rise unless global stocks fall further.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been a generally positive development in stocks in the last few months which has contributed to stabilise prices,&quot; Eivind Reiten, chief executive of Hydro Aluminium, said. &quot;There must, however, be further reductions in stocks before we see large changes (in prices) in the future.&quot;</p>
<p>Reiten said he doubted a forecast by London-based analysts Macquarie Equities that aluminium in 1997 would average about 10 percent over levels in 1996 at current stock levels. --Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
